surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Osterhause</surname> <given-names>AD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Fouchier</surname> <given-names>RA</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Global patterns of influenza A virus in wild birds.</article-title><source>Science</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>312</volume>:<fpage>384</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1122438</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16627734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Webster</surname> <given-names>RG</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Peiris</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Chen</surname> <given-names>H</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Guan</surname> <given-names>Y</given-names></string-name> <article-title>H5N1 outbreaks and enzootic influenza.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>12</volume>:<fpage>3</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16494709</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>